<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-13.10%" pitch="-3.45%">
      After Joseph revealed himself, the family was not only forgiven.<break time="500ms"/>
      They were gathered.<break time="500ms"/>
      They were given a place to dwell.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Jacob came down into Egypt with his household.<break time="500ms"/>
      Joseph went up to meet his father and fell on his neck and wept for a long time.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Years of separation were met with tears instead of distance.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The old father who had mourned a torn robe now saw his living son with his own eyes.<break time="500ms"/>
      Sorrow did not disappear, but it was met by mercy in the land of Egypt.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The family settled in Goshen, where Joseph provided bread for them during the famine.<break time="500ms"/>
      The one once sold away now became a source of keeping for those who had wronged him.<break time="1800ms"/>

      This too is part of the slowing mercy of Joseph's life.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not revenge.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not repayment.<break time="500ms"/>
      Provision.<break time="1800ms"/>

      After Jacob died, Joseph's brothers feared that old harm might return upon them.<break time="500ms"/>
      But Joseph spoke again with gentleness.<break time="500ms"/>
      Do not fear.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You meant evil against me, but God meant it for good, to bring it about that many people should be kept alive.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Then he comforted them and spoke kindly to them.<break time="500ms"/>
      The final sound of the story is not bitterness.<break time="500ms"/>
      It is kindness after long pain.<break time="1800ms"/>

      God's care can grow into mercy over many years.<break time="1000ms"/>
      What is gathered by Him can become peace.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You are not forgotten in waiting.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
